def rotate90(matrix):
    n = len(matrix)
    for i in range(n):
        for j in range(i + 1, n):
            matrix[i][j], matrix[j][i] = matrix[j][i], matrix[i][j]
    for row in matrix:
        row.reverse()
    return matrix

m = [[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6], [7, 8, 9]]
assert rotate90(m) == [[7, 4, 1], [8, 5, 2], [9, 6, 3]]
```

Transpose, then reverse each row. For counterclockwise, reverse rows first, then transpose.

